<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Plötzkau</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Plötzkau is a village on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saale">Saale</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxony-anhalt">Saxony-Anhalt</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>, dominated by a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/renaissance">Renaissance</a> castle. In the 1603 partition of Anhalt it became the seat of the small principality of Anhalt-Plötzkau, held by a younger son of Prince Joachim Ernest. When the line inherited Anhalt-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kothen">Köthen</a> in 1665, Plötzkau returned to Anhalt-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bernburg">Bernburg</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/plotzkau.jpg" alt="Plötzkau" width="299" height="299" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Geisterbob · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pl%C3%B6tzkau_in_SLK.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
